@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE DESK TABS, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* Station tab bar (StationDesks.md rule 3): visible aboard on every desk — the keyboard-shortcut
       equivalent for players who'd rather click. Captain (PR-15) leads the bar with its `0` key, ahead
       of Nav's `1`. #330 (owner: "Should the tile buttons even be there when we are not on the ship?"):
       HIDDEN on a surface excursion — the captain is off-ship and the desks are a tube ride away. The
       captain's link to the ship overhead is #327's orbit-comms line, painted across the excursion HUD. *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        @* #1038 · peek-keep: this bar is the one thing peek leaves standing, because the 👁 button on the
           end of it is the labelled way out of the mode. It has been meant to survive since peek was
           written; until now the exemption named it as a direct child of .map-page and #992's flow column
           quietly repealed that. *@
        <div class="desk-tab-bar peek-keep bg-dark bg-opacity-75 rounded p-1">
            @foreach (ShipDesk desk in TabBarOrder)
            {
                @* #1021 · The Galley chip is still on the bar and is no longer a desk — pressing it raises
                   the galley CARD over whatever is showing (and presses again to shut it), so its hint says
                   that rather than promising a screen the band no longer has. #195's law: every control
                   states what pressing it will do. It never lights, because nothing it does makes it the
                   desk you are sitting at — the tab bar goes on carrying exactly one lit tab. *@
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm desk-tab @(_activeDesk == desk ? "btn-info" : "btn-outline-light")"
                        title="@(desk == ShipDesk.Galley
                                 ? "Open the galley over this desk — the news wire and the rum locker (press again to shut it)"
                                 : $"Switch to the {DeskLabel(desk)} desk")"
                        @onclick="() => SwitchDeskFromClick(desk)">
                    @DeskKeyLabel(desk) @DeskLabel(desk)
                </button>
            }
            @* Owner request: temporarily clear every panel to read the map, and back. Toggles the
               .map-peek class (CSS fades the overlays, click passes through to the canvas). Hotkey ` .
               #1038 · While peeking, this button IS the way out, so it says so in words and names the key
               that also works — #195's law that every control states what pressing it will do, and the
               shell wave's rule that a way out is visible AND worded. *@
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm desk-tab @(_peekMap ? "btn-warning" : "btn-outline-light")"
                    title="@(_peekMap
                             ? "Bring the panels back — or press Esc (` toggles too)"
                             : "Peek at the map — hide the panels (` toggles, Esc brings them back)")"
                    @onclick="TogglePeekMapFromClick">
                @(_peekMap ? "👁 Show panels (Esc)" : "👁 Peek")
            </button>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    // ── WHAT THESE PARAMETERS ARE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // #251 item 1 · Every [Parameter] below carries a member of the page under THE MEMBER'S OWN NAME —
    // a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate with its own signature, a variable the
    // page's `@if` binds arrives under the name the `@if` gave it. That is the whole trick of this
    // refactor: it is what let the markup above move out of Map.razor without a single character of it
    // changing, and what lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as they read it
    // when it lived in the page. A parameter that needs saying more than that says it on its own line.

    [Parameter] public ShipDesk _activeDesk { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public bool _peekMap { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public Func<ShipDesk, string> DeskKeyLabel { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<ShipDesk, string> DeskLabel { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<ShipDesk, Task> SwitchDeskFromClick { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public ShipDesk[] TabBarOrder { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<Task> TogglePeekMapFromClick { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
